scribe a  large variety of phenomena and I really  don't know any other language it would  be so appropriate for describing design  spaces as a Wolfram language so as I  explained these spaces can be just  unimaginably vast you know a few  parameters and you've got a huge  combinatorial explosion but they can  contain very interesting particular  designs and the only way to find out  what's in there is to go out and explore  them so you got to have people exploring  them so my proposal was that well from  research should create this website  called the Wolfram design space and we  would organize design spaces that are  charted and mapped and that this would  serve as an ongoing source of ideas or  material or just cool cool visuals  whatever so there would be four ways to  participate submitting exploring rating  and browsing so of course the first step  would be for people to submit design  spaces and really a lot of them are just  very much like demonstrations of things  that are submitted to demonstrations but  this site would bring us some additional  support to this exploration aspect and  then you could come to the site Explorer  spaces that other people is submitted  and plant flags at interesting locations  in the design space so that way we start  to map out what these designs places  look like and where the interesting  things in them are and then you could  also come and look at the things that  people have found and like them or not  so that you start to get a feeling for  what the terrain looks like not only  where the interesting things are but how  interesting they are  and then finally you might come to the  to the site just to see what's there the  interesting stuff that's there just to  get inspiration you might want to take  me to the site to elaborate to make a  logo for example or you might come to  the site and this was the the motivation  for bringing this up again the site  might be a repository for parametric 3d  designs so you might come there to  customize a design and 3d printed so for  the design world I think this would  provide several things that provides an  infrastructure for this idea of social  exploration of design spaces it promotes  the idea of a design space is a thing to  be designed in itself and I'll get to  that a little more later it promotes the  concept of crowd-sourced social  exploration design space creating  communities of people that are exploring  these things Anakin serve as a resource  for just interesting material I think we  should be doing this because we have the  technology to do it right primarily the  Wolfram language and we have the  experience to do it right because we've  been collecting experience with CDF with  Wolfram community with demonstrations  Wolfram cloud all these aspects are  really important and I think this is  uncolonized internet territory I don't  know of any space of any sites that  attempt to to support this ok so my  interest is in primarily graphic design  and 3d sculptural design and  particularly in design spaces that are  intentionally designed to to be  surprising to be unpredictable to have  interesting things out there defined  when you're going to explore them but  there are many different varieties  possible varieties of design spaces both  in the domain of things that are in the  design space and the way the design  space is constructed for what purpose so  let me just go through some examples  spaces of dimensioned structures is a  possibility so in contrast of the design  space that I described before if I tell  you the dimensions of the phone case you  can probably imagine what  look like right it's not it's not a huge  leap of imagination but there's still a  role for social exploration here because  you can crowdsource having people you  know put on all the right dimensions for  all the different kinds of phones there  are and you know planning flag this is  the iphone case this is the galaxy case  whatever and I think architect